  "what_this_is": "The exact set of committed grading cost ledgers the figures in that entry were computed from. Every count there -- ledgers, rows, distinct_call_ids, duplicate_rows, and the 5.6-sol call and token figures built on them -- is a measurement of these 33 files and of nothing else.",
  "why_pinned_rather_than_walked": "The entry is a measurement of a corpus at a moment, not a description of the repository as it stands. Recomputing it from a live walk of data/grades made those two the same thing, so every legitimate new receipt turned the counts red: the 2026-09-07 smoke published a 33rd ledger and #448 had to hand-edit three numbers to restore green, having first confirmed the 5.6-sol figures were unchanged. The next honoured smoke would have done it again. Pinning the list moves the check onto what the counts were actually protecting -- that no file this measurement rests on has been deleted, truncated or rewritten -- and lets a 34th ledger arrive without touching anything here. Growing this snapshot is a deliberate act: re-measure, re-read the prose, regenerate this file and restate its digest in the entry.",
  "how_to_verify": "Each sha256 below is of the ledger's bytes as committed. batch-runner/tests/test_the_grading_ledger_no_longer_dies_with_the_runner.py recomputes every figure in the entry from exactly these paths, checks each digest, and separately checks that nothing here has vanished from the tree.",
